  "seoBody": "<p>TrueContext is the platform that used to be called <strong>ProntoForms</strong>. This is a <strong>TrueContext alternative UK</strong> teams can buy with no annual commitment.</p><p>We are fair. We say where TrueContext is the better tool.</p><div class=\"key-takeaways\"><strong>Key takeaways</strong><ul><li>TrueContext is the platform formerly called ProntoForms. Same product, new name.</li><li>It is a strong enterprise tool: guided offline workflows, dispatching, conditional logic and PDF, DOCX or XLSX output.</li><li>It is best at connecting to Salesforce, ServiceNow and similar systems.</li><li>The entry tier is $400 a month for the team, billed annually. Higher tiers are quote-only.</li><li>That is a year's commitment before you know if your team will use it.</li><li>Quickler has one price, bills monthly, runs in WhatsApp and fills in your own report.</li><li>If inspections must land inside an enterprise system, TrueContext is the right tool. Quickler is not.</li></ul></div><h2>What TrueContext does well</h2><p>It has guided workflows, offline working, dispatching, conditional logic, and PDF, DOCX or XLSX output.</p><p>Its real strength is integration. Salesforce, ServiceNow and others connect, so a finished job can update your system of record without retyping.</p><h2>An annual commitment, and a quote to ask for</h2><p>The published entry point is the Digital tier. It is 400 US dollars a month for the whole team, billed annually. The two tiers above, Intelligent and Elite, are custom priced. TrueContext says it is not a per-user-per-month tool. Price depends on size and complexity.</p><p>So you commit for a year before you know if your team will use it. And you need a sales call to compare cost.</p><p>It is also an app each person installs and logs into. That is where use drops off.</p><h2>Direct comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>TrueContext</th><th>Quickler</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>What the worker opens</td><td>The TrueContext app, installed, with a login</td><td>WhatsApp or Telegram, already on the phone</td></tr><tr><td>Pricing shape</td><td>From $400 a month, billed annually; higher tiers quote-only</td><td>£75 per phone number a month, monthly in arrears</td></tr><tr><td>Commitment</td><td>Annual</td><td>None, cancel any time</td></tr><tr><td>The report you get</td><td>PDF, DOCX or XLSX from their templates</td><td>Your own Word or PDF report, filled in</td></tr><tr><td>Enterprise integration</td><td>Salesforce, ServiceNow and more</td><td>Not an integration platform</td></tr><tr><td>Free trial</td><td>None published</td><td>14 days, everything unlocked, no card needed to start</td></tr></tbody></table><p>TrueContext's current prices should be checked on their own pricing page before you decide. Ours is on <a href=\"/pages/pricing.html\">our pricing page</a> and does not move.</p><h2>Questions, answered</h2><h3>Is TrueContext the same as ProntoForms?</h3><p>Yes. TrueContext is the platform formerly known as ProntoForms. The new name did not change the product or how it is sold.</p><h3>How much does TrueContext cost?</h3><p>The published entry tier, Digital, starts at 400 US dollars a month for the whole team, billed annually. The Intelligent and Elite tiers are custom priced. Their page says it is not a per-user-per-month tool and that price depends on size and complexity.</p><h3>What does Quickler charge instead?</h3><p>£75 a month for each phone number on the account. Reports, the dashboard, sharing and downloads are free for everyone else. We bill monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit. No annual commitment.</p><h3>What is TrueContext better at?</h3><p>Enterprise integration. Salesforce, ServiceNow and similar systems connect, so a finished job updates your system of record. If your inspections must land inside an enterprise platform, TrueContext is built for it and Quickler is not.</p><h3>Does Quickler need an annual contract?</h3><p>No. We bill monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit. You can stop whenever you like. Start with a 14-day free trial. Everything is unlocked and you need no card to start.</p>",
